Z||000000||Hybrid2M6||11-27-2001||01:19 AM||||I'm thinking of selling my Fiero. I know... I will probably regret it in a few years, but right now I cannot afford everything I had planned to do with it. Just wondering what I should ask for it. <BR>Here's the specs-<BR>1986 SE 2.5L 4cyl 76,xxx AT Red/Gray<BR>Interior-I'd give it an 8 out of 10<BR>-Pioneer tape deck/removable face <BR>-Pioneer 4x6's<BR>-Kenwood 4x10's<BR>-Sagging headliner<BR>-Painted red accents & red mood lights<BR>-Manual looking AT shift knob<BR>Exterior 8 of 10 also, for scratches and damageon drivers side hood and fender(8" tear)<BR>-Wheels (optional) American Racing 16x7's and 17x7.5's-paid$1200 4=16x7's with Ziex's and $600 2=17x7.5's with azenis<BR>-Tires Falken Ziex's(front) and Azenis(rear)<BR>-Two spare 16x7's with Ziex on them (rear)<BR>-JSP adjustable touring wing-paid $180+$140 paint<BR>Please help with the price as I'm hoping to sell it to get a new car this spring/summer. Don't ask what kind of car cuz you probably don't want to know. LOL<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/customgfx.jpg"> <BR>1986 SE IronDuke<BR>Adjustable Touring Wing<BR>American Racing Carrera's<BR> -225/50VR16 Falken Ziex 502<BR> -225/45ZR17 Falken Azenis<BR>Cleared and Painted(red) Tail lights||||reg||5
